L,lfq="Printer.add_indent: Not_found",lfx=[0,m],lfy=[0,jp],lfA=[0,"- **checkbox** \xe2\x80\x94 Toggle UI for boolean literals."],lfB=[0,"- **slider** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (integer)."],lfC=[0,"- **sliderf** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (floating-point)."],lfD=[0,"- **card** \xe2\x80\x94 **Playing-card** editor: a tuple `(Suit, Rank)` such as `(Hearts, Ace)` or a list of those tuples. **Not** for records, modules, or `{ let \xe2\x80\xa6; \xe2\x80\xa6 }` blocks."],lfE=[0,"- **livelit** \xe2\x80\x94 Custom livelit projector for structured literal editing."],lfF=[0,"- **text** \xe2\x80\x94 Multiline string literal editor."],lfG=[0,"- **table** \xe2\x80\x94 Spreadsheet-style editor for a **list of labeled tuples** sharing the same labels; the labels become column headers. Attaches off the **elaborated** form, so it can apply where the surface syntax alone is not yet a table."],lfH=[0,"- **csv** \xe2\x80\x94 CSV **file import** UI. Attaches only when the definition is the **empty list** `[]`; after placement, import fills it with row/tuple syntax. Non-empty lists (e.g. `[1, 2, 3]`) **cannot** take this projector."],lfI=[0,"- **keybinding** \xe2\x80\x94 Key-capture editor for a string literal holding a keyboard shortcut; records the next chord pressed and commits it as the literal."],lfJ=[0,"- **color** \xe2\x80\x94 Color picker for an `Oklch(l, c, h)` literal: a swatch plus lightness, chroma and hue sliders. Attaches only to that constructor applied to three float literals."],lfK=[0,0,0],lfL=[0,m,[0,"These are alternative UIs for literals and structured values that may already appear in code.",0]],lfM=[0,"### Livelits (menu projectors)",0],lfO=[0,m,0],lfP=[0,m,[0,"### Syntax projector tools (Filbert)",[0,"`place_syntax_projector(kind, paths)`, `remove_syntax_projector(paths)`, and `toggle_syntax_projector(kind, paths)` apply **syntax projector** UIs to the term selected by each path.",[0,"`kind` must be a menu projector name (`fold`, `slider`, `sliderf`, `check`, `text`, `card`, `csv`, `table`, `livelit`) \xe2\x80\x94 not `probe` or `statics` (those use the probe/statics tools).",[0,m,[0,"**CRITICAL \xe2\x80\x94 livelits are not automatic:** Ordinary Hazel code (`let speed = 50`, `let is_active = true`, list literals, records) renders as **plain text** until you call **`place_syntax_projector`**.",[0,'If the user asks how livelits work, or wants sliders/checkboxes/CSV editors/text boxes, you **must** call `place_syntax_projector` with the right `kind` on each binding path (e.g. `slider` on `"speed"`, `check` on `"is_active"`, `text` on `"message"`, `csv` only when the RHS is `[]`, `card` only on playing-card tuples/lists\xe2\x80\x94see livelit lines above; nested paths like `"config/volume"`).',[0,"**Never** describe interactive widgets as present based only on `insert_*`, `update_*`, or other edit tools \xe2\x80\x94 that is false unless the matching `place_syntax_projector` calls succeeded.",[0,m,0]]]]]]]]],lfQ=iF(["## Projectors and the agent view",m,"### Fold (`\xe2\x8b\xb1`)","A **fold** is a collapsed definition in the GUI: the definition shows as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (not source text).","Use `expand` / `collapse` (see **Paths** and **View Tools** above).",m,"### Runtime probe refractor","The **probe** refractor attaches to a binding and shows evaluated values in the agent view (e.g. `expr \xe2\x89\xa1 value`).","Tools: `place_probe`, `remove_probe`, `toggle_probe`.",m,"### Statics refractor (type overlay)","The **statics** refractor shows a type ascription overlay in the GUI (offside type cell) for human clarity.","It does not change program text; the agent\xe2\x80\x99s printed context may not mirror the overlay unless printing is extended.",m]),lfR=[0,"**Projectors**: **Folds** display as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (collapsed defs; expand/collapse in the full prompt).",[0,"**Refractors** overlay bindings: **probes** show runtime values (`\xe2\x89\xa1` in context); **statics** add a type overlay in the GUI.",[0,"**Livelits** are alternate UIs for literals (checkbox, slider/sliderf, text, card, csv, table, livelit, plus fold in the menu).",[0,"**Agent tools**: `place_syntax_projector` / `remove_syntax_projector` / `toggle_syntax_projector` (see full prompt).",[0,"Full detail lives in Filbert\xe2\x80\x99s live system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** section (this excerpt may be truncated).",0]]]]],lfX=[0,m],lfW="Editor.Meta.t_of_yojson",lfV="Editor.Meta.yojson_of_t",lfU="Editor.Meta.t_of_sexp",lfS="Editor.Meta.sexp_of_t",lf5=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],lf4=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],lf6=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],lf2=[0,"Empty hole"],lf1=hv,lf0=[0,"Missing operator"],lfY=[0,0,1],lfZ=[0,0,0],lf7=[0,[0,lg,[0,S,[0,[0,b6,[0,i,jI]],[0,[0,kn,[0,S,[0,[0,lN,[0,S,[0,oUy,oUx]]],0]]],[0,[0,hT,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lN],0]]],0]]]]],0],lf8=dW,lf9=[0,cu,[0,i,bra]],lf_=eP,lf$=[0,b6,[0,i,eP]],lga=[0,[0,lg,[0,S,[0,[0,b6,[0,i,jI]],[0,[0,kn,[0,S,[0,[0,lN,[0,S,[0,oUA,oUz]]],0]]],[0,[0,hT,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lN],0]]],0]]]]],0],lgb=dW,lgc=[0,cu,[0,i,box]],lgd=eP,lge=[0,b6,[0,i,eP]],lgf=[0,[0,lg,[0,S,[0,[0,b6,[0,i,jI]],[0,[0,kn,[0,S,[0,[0,lN,[0,S,[0,oUC,oUB]]],0]]],[0,[0,hT,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lN],0]]],0]]]]],0],lgg=dW,lgh=[0,cu,[0,i,bmP]],lgi=eP,lgj=[0,b6,[0,i,eP]],lgx=[0,1],lgu=[0,MT],lgv=[0,dm],lgw=eL,lgs=[0,40],lgr=[0,J_],lgt=m,lgq=[0,0],lgn=[0,jp],lgo=dm,lgp=eL,lgk=bpK,lgl=dRn,lgm=b5U,lgy=[0,0],lgC=[0,0],lgE=[0,1],lgD=[0,m],lg8="Warning: using backup text! Serialization may be for an older version of Hazel.",lg6="persistence load",lg7="PARSE FAILED (persistence load): loading empty buffer",lg3=[0,1],lg4=[0,0],lg5=[0,0],lg1=eL,lg2=bk_,lgZ=eL,lg0=dCY,lgF=[0,[18,[1,[0,[11,d,0],d]],[11,aV,0]],aW],lgG=t3,lgH=[0,[18,[1,[0,0,m]],[2,0,[11,y,[17,[0,a,1,0],0]]]],z],lgI=[0,[3,0,0],aD],lgJ=[0,[17,0,0],v],lgK=[0,[12,59,[17,[0,a,1,0],0]],B],lgL=ajO,lgM=[0,[18,[1,[0,0,m]],[2,0,[11,y,[17,[0,a,1,0],0]]]],z],lgN=[0,[3,0,0],aD],lgO=[0,[17,0,0],v],lgP=[0,[17,[0,a,1,0],[12,az,[17,0,0]]],aX],lgX=ajO,lgY=t3,lgV=ajO,lgW=t3,lgT=[0,ajO],lgU=[0,t3],l